    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 76.13 efficiency score leads our starting nine. **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a highly favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker; the combination of a 10% park boost and the aggressive upside of his placement in the #2 hole makes him our highest-floor play. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (69.49) remains a priority start, buoyed by a significant 14% platoon edge against Landen Roupp and favorable wind conditions that could turn fly balls into counting stats. While **Corbin Carroll** (70.41) continues to be an automatic start, the team is banking on his elite sprint speed to mitigate the scarcity of the stolen base category, even as we wait for final lineup confirmation to lock in his exact role.\n\nWe are monitoring several volatile spots, particularly regarding **Jose Caballero** (58.43) and **Brice Turang** (55.41). **Jose Caballero** faces a high-variance matchup against Shane Bieber, where his 19% SP skill advantage is tempered by a poor platoon split; conversely, **Brice Turang** faces a difficult challenge against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, but our projections remain optimistic due to an 8% boost for his assumed spot at the top of the order and favorable wind. On the bench, **Travis Bazzana** (50.19) was the most difficult exclusion, falling just short of the threshold. While **Travis Bazzana** benefited from a platoon advantage, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher raw projection and positional utility of our current infield starters. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that all lineups are currently pending. We are keeping a close eye on **Gabriel Moreno** (56.39) and **Isaac Paredes** (59.26); while **Isaac Paredes** faces a tough arm in George Kirby, his 9% platoon boost keeps him in the utility slot for now. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**\u2014to preserve game caps, and we remain in a holding pattern regarding the injured **James Wood** until he can rejoin the active roster. We are positioned to chase upside, but we are prepared to pivot quickly if the official batting orders negatively impact the projected points for **Austin Riley** or **Henry Bolte**.",
